# Disposable client. Prepare two draft risks: one with an asset at 1 ruble/hour and one without.
# Copy IDs and versions from responses after each mutation. Use an unrelated user with assess_risk for the 403 case.
@public = https://localhost:7224/api/v1/public
@provider = https://localhost:7224/api/v1/provider
@admin = REPLACE_ADMIN_TOKEN
@outsider = REPLACE_UNRELATED_ASSESSOR_TOKEN
@risk = REPLACE_DRAFT_RISK_WITH_ASSET
@manualRisk = REPLACE_DRAFT_RISK_WITHOUT_ASSET
@riskVersion = REPLACE_RISK_VERSION
@scaleVersion = REPLACE_PUBLISHED_SCALE_ID
@assetVersion = REPLACE_ASSET_VERSION
@settingsVersion = REPLACE_ACCEPTANCE_SETTINGS_VERSION
@primary = REPLACE_PRIMARY_PROCESS_ID
@secondary = REPLACE_OTHER_PROCESS_ID
@likelihood5 = be7d17a4-a396-4518-b240-b94822ce9105

### Embedded matrix excludes the zero-weight axes and still exposes zero levels in its catalog
GET {{public}}/risk-assessment-settings/matrix
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

> {%
    client.test("5 by 5 positive matrix", function () {
        client.assert(response.body.scores.length === 5);
        client.assert(response.body.scores.every(row => row.length === 5 && row.every(score => score > 0)));
        client.assert(response.body.likelihoodLevels[0].weight === 0);
    });
%}

### Before publishing thresholds, preview fails with 409 RISK_SCALE_REQUIRED
POST {{public}}/risks/{{manualRisk}}/assessments/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"likelihoodLevelId":"{{likelihood5}}","lossAmount":0}

### Publish initial thresholds. Use returned version.id for later requests
PUT {{provider}}/risk-assessment-settings/impact-scale
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"minimums":[1,10,100,200.01,1000]}

### Mixed downtime is 200.005 hours; HALF_UP produces 200.01 and weight 4
POST {{public}}/risks/{{risk}}/assessments/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"likelihoodLevelId":"{{likelihood5}}","downtimeWeeks":1,"downtimeDays":1,"downtimeHours":8.005}

> {%
    client.test("Mixed downtime rounds before classification", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200);
        client.assert(response.body.assessment.downtimeTotalHours === 200.005);
        client.assert(response.body.assessment.lossAmount === 200.01);
        client.assert(response.body.assessment.riskScore === 20);
        client.assert(response.body.acceptanceLevel === "TREATMENT_REQUIRED");
    });
%}

### Zero stays in assessment history and has no positive matrix cell
POST {{public}}/risks/{{manualRisk}}/assessments/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"likelihoodLevelId":"{{likelihood5}}","lossAmount":0}

> {%
    client.test("Valid zero loss", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200);
        client.assert(response.body.assessment.riskScore === 0);
    });
%}

### One cent below the boundary still belongs to the previous range
POST {{public}}/risks/{{manualRisk}}/assessments/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"likelihoodLevelId":"{{likelihood5}}","lossAmount":200.00}

> {%
    client.test("Inclusive previous range", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200);
        client.assert(response.body.assessment.riskScore === 15);
    });
%}

### 400 rejects client-chosen derived values
POST {{public}}/risks/{{manualRisk}}/assessments/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"likelihoodLevelId":"{{likelihood5}}","lossAmount":10,"riskScore":25}

### 403 refuses an unrelated assessor
POST {{public}}/risks/{{risk}}/assessments/preview
Authorization: Bearer {{outsider}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"likelihoodLevelId":"{{likelihood5}}","downtimeHours":200.005}

### Run two copies concurrently with the same versions. One returns 200 and one returns 409
POST {{public}}/risks/{{risk}}/assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version":"{{riskVersion}}","scaleVersionId":"{{scaleVersion}}","assetVersion":"{{assetVersion}}","inputs":{"likelihoodLevelId":"{{likelihood5}}","downtimeWeeks":1,"downtimeDays":1,"downtimeHours":8.005}}

### After first assessment, the prior passport update scenario with a fresh version returns RISK_PASSPORT_LOCKED
GET {{public}}/risks/{{risk}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

> {%
    client.test("The assessed passport is read-only even for the administrator", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200);
        client.assert(response.body.passportEditable === false);
    });
%}

### Send split and treat concurrently with the same risk version. Exactly one choice succeeds
POST {{public}}/risks/{{risk}}/split
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version":"{{riskVersion}}","processIds":["{{primary}}","{{secondary}}"],"primaryProcessId":"{{secondary}}"}

### Competing decision
POST {{public}}/risks/{{risk}}/treat
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version":"{{riskVersion}}"}

### Technical recalculation creates a new version and preserves the successful responseMode
PUT {{provider}}/risk-assessment-settings/impact-scale
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version":"{{scaleVersion}}","minimums":[0,20,120,220,1000]}

### A conflict forced on one assessment insert must roll back this entire operation (including scale and outbox)
GET {{public}}/risks/{{risk}}/assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Applying routing thresholds keeps the IDs and inputs of all assessment versions
PUT {{provider}}/risk-assessment-settings/acceptance
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version":"{{settingsVersion}}","ownerMaxScore":5,"directorMaxScore":10,"ceoMaxScore":19,"applyToExisting":true}

### Historical range remains readable after publication of a newer scale
GET {{public}}/risk-assessment-settings/impact-scale/{{scaleVersion}}
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Use a new active risk without a selected mode. An administrator can accept TREATMENT_REQUIRED
POST {{public}}/risks/{{risk}}/accept
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version":"{{riskVersion}}"}

### For an active risk with an empty mode, the selector includes eligible processes across directorates
GET {{public}}/risks/{{risk}}/split/processes
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Save against an older asset version after changing the rate. Expect 409 and no new assessment
POST {{public}}/risks/{{risk}}/assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"version":"{{riskVersion}}","scaleVersionId":"{{scaleVersion}}","assetVersion":"{{assetVersion}}","inputs":{"likelihoodLevelId":"{{likelihood5}}","downtimeHours":200.005}}
